        "decision-making, while",
        "Oxford",
        "itself",
        "reinforced something even more valuable — the patience",
        "to",
        "resist",
        "easy",
        "answers.",
        "It strengthened her belief that the most meaningful decisions are rarely made quickly. They emerge through careful observation and",
        "intellectual curiosity. That",
        "curiosity",
        "extends",
        "well",
        "beyond her",
        "formal",
        "education.",
        "Vedika",
        "reads extensively across history, philosophy, behavioural",
        "science,",
        "leadership,",
        "and organisational",
        "psychology,",
        "convinced that the most valuable ideas are often discovered where disciplines intersect rather than where they remain isolated.",
        "A Consultant by Temperament",
        "Long",
        "before",
        "corporate",
        "appointments became",
        "part",
        "of",
        "her",
        "professional journey,",
        "Vedika",
        "had",
        "already",
        "begun doing",
        "what",
        "came",
        "naturally",
        "to",
        "her: helping",
        "people",
        "think",
        "differently. Founders,",
        "entrepreneurs,",
        "operators, and",
        "leadership",
        "teams",
        "increasingly found",
        "themselves",
        "seeking",
        "her perspective—not because she claimed to",
        "have",
        "every",
        "answer,",
        "but",
        "because she asked questions that encouraged organisations",
        "to",
        "see",
        "their",
