      "paragraphs": [
        "In Focus",
        "A Confluence of Culture, Quality and Economic Growth",
        "Indian GI Products",
        "The",
        "Geographical",
        "Indication",
        "(GI)",
        "products",
        "in",
        "India",
        "have witnessed",
        "significant",
        "boost",
        "and",
        "gained",
        "tremendous momentum in recent years. With the country's rich cultural heritage and diverse regional traditions, increasing number of products are getting recognized and registered as GI. From traditional",
        "handicrafts",
        "like",
        "Kanchipuram",
        "silk",
        "sarees",
        "and Madhubani paintings to agricultural products like Darjeeling tea and Nagpur oranges, the GI tag has become a badge of authenticity and quality assurance. The Indian government's efforts to promote and protect these products through legal frameworks, awareness campaigns and marketing initiatives have played a crucial role in their rising popularity.",
        "Arunachal Pradesh Angnyat Millet",
        "Arunachal Pradesh Angnyat Millet is a unique millet cultivated in the picturesque landscapes of",
        "Arunachal",
        "Pradesh,",
        "India.",
        "Grown",
        "at",
        "high altitudes amidst the pristine surroundings of the Himalayas. This millet thrives in the region's favourable",
        "climatic",
        "conditions,",
        "rich",
        "soil",
        "and traditional farming practices. Angnyat Millet is cherished not only for its distinct nutty flavour and nutritional benefits but also for its cultural significance, deeply ingrained in the culinary traditions",
        "of",
        "the",
        "indigenous",
        "communities",
        "of Arunachal Pradesh. The product was granted geographic indication (GI) status Millet on January 22, 2024. To create domestic and global demand for millets and to",
        "provide",
        "nutritional",
        "food",
        "to",
        "the",
        "people, the",
        "Government",
        "of",
        "India",
        "proposed",
        "to",
        "the United Nations to declare the year 2023 as the",
        "International",
        "Year",
        "of",
        "Millets.",
        "Moreover, the",
        "recognition",
        "of",
        "Angnyat",
        "Millet",
        "as",
        "GI product",
        "underscores",
        "its",
        "value",
        "in",
        "promoting local",
        "economies",
        "and",
        "fostering",
        "community empowerment, in line with the goals of the international initiative."
      ],
