      "printedPage": 9,
      "paragraphs": [
        "In Focus",
        "racticing mindfulness creates strong individuals who are self-aware and resilient. Join this journey of understanding as we delve into insights from the visionary founder Dr Manimekalai Mohan on mindfulness in education. Discover its impact on learning, teaching, and parenting.",
        "How does mindfulness support in finding one’s purpose of life?",
        "Mindfulness serves as a guiding force in aligning with one’s ‘Ikigai’, the Japanese concept of finding purpose and joy in life. By cultivating mindfulness, individuals gain heightened awareness of their passions, strengths, and the broader needs of the world — integral components of Ikigai. This heightened consciousness allows for a more intentional exploration of one’s purpose and a clearer understanding of how personal fulfilment aligns with the greater good, creating a harmonious blend of personal satisfaction and societal contribution.",
        "How can students benefit from practicing mindful learning?",
        "Mindful learning transforms the student experience by encouraging presence, deep engagement and strategic self-care. In academic pursuits, staying fully present during lectures, taking purposeful breaks, mindful eating habits and connecting with study materials on a profound level become paramount. By incorporating mindfulness into their study routines, students not only enhance their academic performance but also nurture a lifelong love for learning, making education a fulfilling and enriching part of their lives.",
        "Why is the young age crucial for practicing mindfulness in personal development?",
        "The formative years of youth serve as a critical period",
        "a lifelong commitment to learning. Moreover, mindful habits established during youth create a framework for making informed choices, thereby shaping a purposeful and meaningful life.",
        "What are the key aspects of mindful teaching in an educational setting?",
        "Mindful teaching is a holistic approach that transforms the educational landscape by emphasising the teacher’s presence, adaptability and awareness of students’ needs. Fully present in the classroom, mindful educators prioritise cultivating an inclusive and positive atmosphere. This involves active listening to students, understanding their individual learning styles and tailoring teaching methods accordingly. The emphasis is not only on academic growth but also on nurturing the overall well-being of students, creating an environment that fosters both academic success and personal development.",
        "How can mindfulness enhance the parent-child relationship in mindful parenting?",
        "Mindful parenting transcends conventional approaches by emphasising being fully present, understanding, non-¬judgemental and responding thoughtfully to a child’s needs. By practicing mindfulness, parents create a space for open communication, active listening, and genuine empathy. Patience becomes a cornerstone, allowing parents to navigate challenges with a calm and composed demeanour. Mindful parenting involves not only acknowledging a child’s emotions but also validating them, contributing to a deeper and more connected relationship. Through mindful parenting, caregivers can instil valuable life skills in their children, paving the way for emotional intelligence, resilience, trust culture and a strong parent-child bond that extends well into the future.",
        "for cultivating mindfulness in personal development. This stage is pivotal for building healthy relationships, fostering academic growth and exploring diverse interests. This foundation becomes instrumental in navigating life’s challenges and lays the groundwork for",
        "MINDFULNESS",
        "FOR BLISSFUL LIVING",
        "Dr. Manimekalai Mohan",
        "Founder & Managing Trustee SSVM Institutions, Coimbatore, Tamil Nadu"
      ],
